  "final_answer": "I now have comprehensive information about Copilot Pro (the plan for individuals, formerly \"Copilot Individual\"). Let me provide my final answer.\n\n## Answer\n\n### Cost of Copilot Individual (Copilot Pro)\n**$120 USD per year** ($10 USD per user/month × 12 months)\n\nNote: GitHub's plan for individual users was rebranded from \"GitHub Copilot Individual\" to **\"Copilot Pro\"** in their current plans.\n\n### Features of Copilot Pro\n\n**1. Inline Code Completions & Chat**\n- Inline code suggestions (real-time completions in supported IDEs)\n- Next edit suggestions\n- Copilot Chat in IDEs (VS Code, Visual Studio, JetBrains, etc.)\n- Inline chat\n- Slash commands\n- Copilot Chat in GitHub (web)\n- Copilot Chat in GitHub Mobile\n- Copilot Chat in Windows Terminal\n- Copilot Chat skills in IDEs\n\n**2. Access to AI Models**\n- A selection of frontier and standard AI models including:\n  - Claude (Haiku 4.5, Sonnet 4.6, Sonnet 5)\n  - Gemini (Flash 3.5–3.7)\n  - GPT-5 family variants\n  - Grok models\n\n**3. AI Agents**\n- Copilot cloud agent (assign tasks to Copilot that work autonomously)\n- Agent mode (in IDEs)\n- Copilot code review (full PR review, not just \"Review selection\")\n- Model Context Protocol (MCP) support\n- Third-party Agents (public preview) — e.g., Claude Code, Codex\n\n**4. GitHub AI Credits**\n- Base: 1,000 monthly credits\n- Flex allotment: 500 monthly credits\n- **Total: 1,500 monthly AI credits** (~$15 value)\n\n**5. Platform Support**\n- VS Code, Visual Studio, JetBrains, Eclipse, Xcode, etc.\n- CLI support\n- GitHub (web and mobile)\n\n### Summary\nCopilot Pro (the Individual plan) costs **$120 USD per year** ($10/month) and provides unlimited code completions, Chat in IDEs and GitHub, access to multiple AI models, all agents (including cloud agent and code review), and 1,500 monthly AI credits. It is designed for individual developers needing AI assistance beyond the Free tier's limits (2,000 completions/month on entry-level models only).",
